} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "31 July –  2 August 1952"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/375"} "Helsingin Uimastadion, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/5337"} "33 from 17 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The 400m Freestyle was destined to be a clash between Hungary, the USA and Denmark. The return of world record holder " [:a {:href "/athletes/46268"} "Ragnhild Hveger-Andersen"] ", after a sixteen year Olympic absence, added to the talents of European champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/46251"} "Grete Andersen"] "  meant that Denmark would be well represented whilst a trio of talented Hungarians and the American pairing of " [:a {:href "/athletes/51078"} "Evelyn Kawamoto"] "  and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51038"} "Carolyn Green"] "  could not be discounted. For nearly 300 metres the impossible seemed about to happened as Hveger-Andersen, at 32 and coming back from a 7 year retirement, held off her younger rivals but her early efforts were in vain as  four swimmers passed her. The gold medal was decided between two Hungarians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/48101"} "Valéria Gyenge"] "  and " [:a {:href "/athletes/45461"} "Éva Novák"] ", with Gyenge edging her more experienced team-mate for the victory."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "586"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48101"} "Valéria Gyenge"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "5:22.6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "5:16.9 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "5:12.1 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:cla